const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const here = `${base}research/governed-agentic-research/ai-in-empirical-se/`;
---

<Base
  title="Jason Cusati — AI across the Empirical-SE Lifecycle: Literature-Gap Table"
  description="For each key source on AI in empirical software engineering research: what it already establishes, where it falls short, how it relates to the proposed chapter, and whether the proposal cites it or positions against it."
>
  <p class="crumbs"><a href={here}>← AI across the empirical-SE lifecycle</a></p>
  <h1>Literature-Gap Table</h1>
  <p class="meta">A derived view of <code>llm/construction/research/literature-gap.md</code> in the chapter repository — the plan's Task 1 table, built from the research store. Bracketed tokens link to the <a href={`${here}sources/`}>source explorer</a>. "Yes — cite" and "position against" are the proposal's intended use, pending citation verification.</p>
  <article class="gap" set:html={html} />
</Base>

<style is:global>
  .crumbs { font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .meta { color: var(--color-muted); font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .gap p { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .gap a.cite { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.78em; color: var(--color-accent); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .gap table { border-collapse: collapse; font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.82rem; margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem; display: block; overflow-x: auto; max-width: 100%; }
  .gap th, .gap td { border: 1px solid var(--color-border); padding: 0.4rem 0.5rem; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; min-width: 9rem; }
  .gap th { background: var(--color-surface); }
  code { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.9em; background: var(--color-surface); padding: 0 0.25em; }
</style>
